# group|when|text
after|!TRACEARR_API_KEY?|Tracearr: open it and create the owner account. Its first page asks for a claim code: TRACEARR_CLAIM_CODE from ~/server/kit/generated-secrets.conf.
after|MEDIA_SERVER=plex,!TRACEARR_API_KEY?|Tracearr: add Plex by signing in with your Plex account, then pick this Mac's server: Connect, or if none of its connections is reachable, Custom URL http://plex-proxy:32400.
after|MEDIA_SERVER=jellyfin,!TRACEARR_API_KEY?|Tracearr: add Jellyfin under Settings → Servers → Connections → Add Server: type Jellyfin, URL http://jellyfin-proxy:8096, and an API key (in Jellyfin: your account (top right) → Dashboard → API Keys → +).
after|MEDIA_SERVER=both,!TRACEARR_API_KEY?|Tracearr: add your servers. Plex: sign in with your Plex account and pick this Mac's server (Connect, or if none of its connections is reachable, Custom URL http://plex-proxy:32400). Jellyfin: Settings → Servers → Connections → Add Server, type Jellyfin, URL http://jellyfin-proxy:8096, and an API key (in Jellyfin: your account (top right) → Dashboard → API Keys → +).
after|!TRACEARR_API_KEY?|Tracearr's Homarr widget: make its API key (Tracearr → Settings → Data & API → API → Generate Key), put it in ~/server/secrets.conf as TRACEARR_API_KEY, and run ./kit install again.
